@startuml
title 5G Signaling: Access Stratum (AS) vs Non-Access Stratum (NAS)

skinparam shadowing false
skinparam participantPadding 10
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
skinparam maxMessageSize 90

actor UE
participant "gNB\n(5G Base Station)" as gNB
participant "AMF\n(Core Control Plane)" as AMF

== Access Stratum (AS) - Radio Control ==

note left of gNB
RRC = Radio Resource Control
end note

UE -> gNB: RRC Setup Request
gNB -> UE: RRC Setup
UE -> gNB: RRC Setup Complete

note right of gNB
AS = UE <-> gNB
Radio access control
Examples: RRC, PDCP, RLC, MAC/PHY
end note

== NAS messages carried inside AS ==
UE -> gNB: NAS: Registration Request\n(encapsulated in RRC/N2 transport)
gNB -> AMF: Forward NAS via N2\n(Initial UE Message)

note right of AMF
NAS = UE <-> AMF
Core control messaging
Examples:
- Registration
- Authentication (5G-AKA)
- NAS Security Mode
- Mobility updates
end note

== NAS Authentication Example ==
AMF -> gNB: NAS: Authentication Request
gNB -> UE: NAS: Authentication Request

UE -> gNB: NAS: Authentication Response
gNB -> AMF: NAS: Authentication Response

== After NAS Security ==
AMF -> gNB: NAS Security Mode Command
gNB -> UE: NAS Security Mode Command
UE -> gNB: NAS Security Mode Complete
gNB -> AMF: NAS Security Mode Complete

note bottom
Key point:
NAS is UE<->AMF logically,
but physically passes through gNB.
gNB forwards NAS like a courier.
end note
@enduml
